00:03:52.299 --> 00:03:53.749
Number four, going to the source.

00:03:53.749 --> 00:03:55.360
I like to go to the source.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:04:00.200
I remember a long time ago when I was getting
contracts with insurance companies, and I

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.450
was constantly talking to all these VPs, Vice
Presidents.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.260
"Oh yeah, we'll try to get a deal for you.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:07.209
Oh yeah, we'll try to get a deal for you,"
and all of a sudden I said, "You know what,

00:04:07.209 --> 00:04:09.170
I'm going straight to the source."

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:13.969
I found that every insurance company CEOs,
I found that all of these guys are human beings,

00:04:13.969 --> 00:04:18.130
like you and I, they have a Linkedin, they
have a contact information.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:21.000
They know people that have information that
I know, so I reached out to them.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.890
Eventually I got ahold of the CEOs.

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:23.890
Direct phone.

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:24.890
I spoke to them.

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:25.890
I said, "Listen, here's who I am.

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:27.080
Here's what I'm looking for.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:28.130
I'm looking for a contract.

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:29.200
I just started a company.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:30.200
I like our company.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.520
When can we get together and talk?"

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:32.520
"Can you come here tomorrow?"

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:33.520
"Yes."

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:36.040
I flew to Chicago, struck up a deal with the
CEO, came back.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:40.230
We had an insurance company to work with because
I went directly to the source.

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:41.500
Many times you got to go straight to the source.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:42.500
Number five.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:43.500
Leverage.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:46.010
Let me tell you what I mean by leverage.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:49.380
Leverage is knowing who has the leverage.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:54.430
I've seen people negotiate with people as
if they have the power, and they don't.

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:56.300
Let me explain.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:05:00.470
Let's just way me and and a bank are having
a problem here together.

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:05.060
The bank has given me $50 million for my business,
okay?

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:08.170
The bank is absolutely upset with me.

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:09.500
We want our $50 million.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:12.920
We've given you $50 million and this is our
$50 million.

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:17.090
If they push me to the edge, I can file bankruptcy.

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:19.370
They'll lose $15 million.

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:21.530
They need to understand leverage here.

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:26.530
They need to make sure I stay in business,
because if I stay in business, I can pay them

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:27.530
back.

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:31.270
That is leverage right there, so you need
to know your position of leverage.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:34.690
Not just necessarily going in and pounding
your fist on the table and saying, "This is

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:36.080
what I demand from you."

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:38.550
If you don't have proper leverage, it will
work against you.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.280
Number six, not listening.

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:41.440
It's pretty simple.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:45.180
Sometimes the whole thing about misinterpretation,
the more you listen, you'll start seeing signs,

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:48.860
and you'll start seeing exactly what's important
to them, and you'll start seeing what they're

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:50.230
not willing to negotiate with.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:53.710
That will help you get to the final decision
sooner.

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:57.650
Number seven, knowing when to walk away, and
when not to walk away.

00:05:57.650 --> 00:06:02.920
I will tell you from personal mistakes, I
have sometimes walked away way too early,

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:04.810
and it cost me millions of dollars.

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:10.050
I have sometimes walked away too late, and
it cost me a lot of hours.

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:11.050
Okay?

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:15.830
From experience, you generally make this thing
tighter where you'll be able to save more

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:20.240
money, make more money, and save more time,
and make more time to do other things.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:24.290
There are times where you're into it, and
you may not like somebody, or you may not

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:26.970
like something that was said, but that doesn't
mean you're not going to do business with

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:27.970
them.

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:31.140
Unpeel it a little bit more, and all of a
sudden, something could happen.

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:33.560
There's sometimes patience is important.

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:36.990
Many time you can tell a deal and say, "Look,
we were just doing a deal," and I told the

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:42.000
guy, "Listen, I want to do this deal, but
I'm not going to do based on these guidelines.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.420
If you have something better, honestly go.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:45.730
I'm just here waiting.

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:47.900
If you want to do some like this, I'm open."

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:51.270
Then we came back two months later, and we
ended up doing a deal, because we were patient

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:52.270
about it.

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:54.240
You need to know your position where you are
with that.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:55.240
Number eight.

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:58.140
Too extreme, too soft, too hard.

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:00.310
You push too hard, you're too soft.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:02.080
If you're too soft, you're showing a weak
position.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:03.730
Maybe your product's not as good.

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:06.610
If you're too hard, maybe the other person
says, "This person's going to be difficult

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:07.610
to do business with."

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:11.610
You to to kind of figure out a way to be balanced
with them while you're dealing with them.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:12.610
Number nine.

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:14.960
Understanding the personality.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:16.740
I was doing a negotiation with this one guy.

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:18.570
He's $100 million guy two weeks ago.

00:07:18.570 --> 00:07:19.770
We're on a call.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.740
He interrupts me, three times on a call.

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:25.240
I don't mind it, but he interrupts me three
times.

00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:29.240
When he interrupted me three times, I interrupted
him and I said, "Listen, I just hope your

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:30.280
understand this.

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:33.110
I have zero problem if you interrupt me.

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:34.110
Okay?

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:35.430
I hope you also don't have a problem if I
interrupt you."

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:37.460
He said, "I have no problem with that."

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:43.390
Our relationship was so good because we both
understood what level we're comfortable and

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:44.880
in negotiation went well.

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:49.800
There are people that will not even interrupt
you until you're done with your sentence,

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:53.360
and then you got to know they're expecting
the same thing in return.

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:56.620
Sometimes you got to read personalities when
you're negotiating on where they're at.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:59.200
Some people are more sensitive than others.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:02.490
When you're dealing with more sensitive people,
if you still want the deal to get done, you

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:04.400
got to be able to read that other human being
better.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:05.400
Number 10.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:07.030
Letting people know how you do business.

00:08:07.030 --> 00:08:10.740
I told this guy ... Mario reminded me this
yesterday, two days ago.

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:14.580
He says, "Pat, you probably said this line
hundreds of times in meetings."

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:18.350
I'll sit with somebody I'm doing business
with, and I want a long-term relationship

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:19.350
with them.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:21.820
I'll tell them, I said, "Listen I'm not looking
for a one night stand.

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:23.580
I'm done with one night stands.

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:25.400
I'm looking for marriage.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:29.932
If you want to marry me, why don't we start
dating, and then from there possible we will

00:08:29.932 --> 00:08:32.579
put a ring on each other, and then one day
we'll get married?

00:08:32.579 --> 00:08:35.669
I'm looking for a marriage, not a one night
stand.

00:08:35.669 --> 00:08:36.669
What are you looking for?"

00:08:36.669 --> 00:08:37.669
"I also want a marriage."

00:08:37.669 --> 00:08:42.030
"Why don't we start solving around this on
how we can make this relationship last a long

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:44.470
time so you make millions, we make millions.

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:45.580
Are you okay with that?"

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:46.580
"Yes."

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:47.890
Explain to people how you do business with
people.

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:49.340
Number 11.

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:50.340
Caring too much.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:52.130
This kind of goes a little bit into the emotion
side.

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:56.830
When you caring too much about the deal because
you have a personal ... Many times a deal

00:08:56.830 --> 00:09:00.790
may not get done just because you care way
too much about the deal.

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:01.790
12.

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:04.010
Focusing only on the money.

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:08.371
There are a lot of negotiation books out there
that want you to get all the money, and all

00:09:08.371 --> 00:09:09.371
this other stuff.

00:09:09.371 --> 00:09:12.720
Listen, I've played that card as well, where
it's all about how much of the money I'm going

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:13.720
to get myself.

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:18.330
Then what happens in this case is that person
walks away.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:19.800
I said this on a call the other day.

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:24.730
I told this guy, I said, "Listen if we do
business, two months later I realize you got

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:28.061
the better end of the deal, you're not going
to get the better version of me, so what do

00:09:28.061 --> 00:09:29.061
you want to do?"

00:09:29.061 --> 00:09:30.700
He says, "Yeah, you're right Pat.

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:31.940
That kind of does make sense.

00:09:31.940 --> 00:09:33.820
Well what can we do for you not to feel that?"

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:35.110
I said, "Well this is my number."

00:09:35.110 --> 00:09:36.860
He says, "Well that's kind of fair."

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:37.910
I said, "Well I want to be able to do this."

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:39.580
I said, "Can you give me this other part?

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:40.580
What about if I wanted this?"

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:44.450
I said, "That's no problem to me, but I want
you to make sure that here's what I'm looking

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:45.670
for."

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:48.460
Negotiating just for the money, there are
some freedoms, and some other things you can

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:51.950
negotiate that may be important to you or
to them, that's more important than the money

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:54.280
part, so don't always just leave it on thee
money side.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:59.280
Number 13, trying to beat the other person.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:05.950
I had somebody that we had in our lives two
years ago, okay.

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:09.150
Every conversation with her, she had to win.

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:14.950
Literally, it was only about beating you in
the conversations.

00:10:14.950 --> 00:10:15.950
I stopped talking.

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:19.480
I'm just sitting there saying, "What do you
want me to talk to you about?

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:21.090
What other conversation do you want the win?

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:22.420
Do you want to win another one?

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:23.420
Keep winning."

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:26.680
There is no point of negotiating with this
person, or even trying to have a relationship

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:30.810
with this person, because it was always about
beating the other person.

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:34.790
It was always about winning the argument,
and there's not a lot that you can do with

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:35.790
that part.

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:38.590
When negotiating with people, you got to know
it can't just be about beating the other person,

00:10:38.590 --> 00:10:41.330
it's about I want to keep doing business,
and this person's going to talk to five other

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:42.330
people.

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:45.010
I want them to come back and want to do business
with me.

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:46.010
Number 14.

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:48.400
Not seeking other options.

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:52.760
Every time somebody at the homme office comes
up to me with a deal, "Pat this is going it

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:53.760
cost us $100,000.

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:55.180
This is going to cost us $600,000.

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:58.010
This is going to cost us $50,000."

00:10:58.010 --> 00:11:01.951
No matter what deal they will come to me with,
I always ask them one question, "How many

00:11:01.951 --> 00:11:03.050
other options do we have?

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:04.850
Do we have three options?"

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:07.100
If it's only one option, no, it's not enough.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:08.100
I want three.

